# .afkignore — per-repo label filter for afk-agent
#
# Copy this file to your repository root as `.afkignore` (drop the `.example`
# suffix). Any open issue carrying a label listed here is dropped from the
# afk-agent plan into the "Ignored (.afkignore)" bucket BEFORE any other
# eligibility check runs — so it stays visible in the plan instead of silently
# disappearing, but is never claimed or implemented.
#
# Syntax (v1, intentionally minimal):
#   - one label per line
#   - lines beginning with `#` are comments
#   - blank lines are ignored
#   - leading/trailing whitespace is stripped
#   - matching is EXACT and CASE-SENSITIVE against the issue's label names
#   - no globs, no regex, no negation
#
# Example: keep human-owned, parked, and untriaged work out of AFK runs.

ready-for-human
needs-info
wontfix
